                <head>PM–47. Editorial Note</head>
                <p>On May 8, 1960, presidential elections were held in Panama to select a successor
                    to President Ernesto de la Guardia, Jr., whose four-year term expired in the
                    autumn. Dr. Roberto F. Chiari was
                    elected the new President of Panama, and he assumed office on October 1, 1960.
                    Documentation concerning the election campaign is in Department of State file
                    719.00.</p>
            </div>
